# it is the one rule on that page this design could plausibly breach, and the
# conclusion is not obvious. Read as it is written -- a TINT is a brand colour
# mixed with white, and the rule keeps a swatch from fading into an
# indeterminate near-white -- nothing here is a tint at all: every colour is a
# full-strength LCh value composited at partial alpha, not a colour diluted with
# white. Read at its loosest, as "no applied colour may contribute less than a
# tenth", the two TEXTURE layers do breach it: measured by deleting each layer
# and re-rendering, the macro grain peaks at 13 parts in 255 and the micro at 20
# -- 5% and 8%. The washes, shades and ramp are all well above.
#
# So: not a violation under the natural reading, a breach under the strictest
# one, and it costs one number to fix if the owner wants it fixed. Said out loud
# rather than resolved unilaterally, because it is his brand and not mine.
